Subject: [PATCH 28/67] =?UTF-8?q?fix(aligram):=20O-02=20=E2=80=94=20launch?=
 =?UTF-8?q?er=20icon=20preview=20uses=20the=20real=20adaptive-icon=20layer?=
 =?UTF-8?q?s?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

LauncherIcon.DEFAULT passed R.mipmap.ic_launcher_aligram for both
background and foreground, so the selector/preview rendered the full
icon twice, layered. It now passes R.drawable
.ic_launcher_aligram_background / .ic_launcher_aligram_foreground — the
same pair mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher_aligram.xml uses, and the same
background/foreground split the old multi-icon enum used. Manifest icon
untouched.
---
 .../main/java/org/telegram/ui/LauncherIconController.java | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/LauncherIconController.java b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/LauncherIconController.java
index 05b4e5fd1..0b932bcbc 100644
--- a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/LauncherIconController.java
+++ b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/LauncherIconController.java
@@ -36,8 +36,14 @@ public class LauncherIconController {
     // --- AliGram: a single launcher icon. The Nagram icon variants were
     // removed from the manifest (BRANDING.md); the selector therefore
     // offers only the original AliGram icon.
+    // O-02 (Phase 3.2): background/foreground are the adaptive-icon layers
+    // (the same pair mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher_aligram.xml uses),
+    // NOT the full icon twice — AppIconsSelectorCell renders background
+    // via setImageResource and foreground via setForeground, so passing
+    // the full icon for both showed it doubled, layered. The manifest
+    // icon itself is untouched.
     public enum LauncherIcon {
-        DEFAULT("DefaultIcon", R.mipmap.ic_launcher_aligram, R.mipmap.ic_launcher_aligram, R.string.AppIconDefault);
+        DEFAULT("DefaultIcon", R.drawable.ic_launcher_aligram_background, R.drawable.ic_launcher_aligram_foreground, R.string.AppIconDefault);
 
         public final String key;
         public final int background;
-- 
